(CHAPTER 2: CRYPTOGRAPHIC VAULT AND DATA PRIVACY STANDARDS) Tj
T*
0 Tc
() Tj
T*
0 Tc
(2.1 SYMMETRIC ENCRYPTION AT REST \(AES-256\)) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(DocuChat implements the Fernet authenticated symmetric cipher suite, which combines AES-128-CBC) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(with HMAC-SHA256 for authenticated message integrity. The system derives high-entropy 256-bit keys) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(using PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 with 200,000 hashing iterations and unique cryptographic salts.) Tj
T*
0 Tc
() Tj
T*
0 Tc
(2.2 ZERO-RETENTION MEMORY SCRUBBING) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(When the user initiates a Zero-Retention Purge:) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(- All encrypted .enc files stored in the .vault directory undergo multi-pass pseudorandom overwrites.) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(- In-memory cryptographic keys and vector embeddings are flushed from volatile memory.) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(- The key fingerprint is regenerated, invalidating prior session context permanently.) Tj
T*
0 Tc
() Tj
T*
0 Tc
(2.3 PII ANONYMIZATION AND REDACTION) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(To safeguard user privacy, DocuChat features an automated Personally Identifiable Information \(PII\) scrubber.) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(Sensitive identifiers including email addresses, telephone numbers, and Social Security Numbers are) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(masked before text context is submitted to the Large Language Model.) Tj
T*
0 Tc
() Tj
T*
0 Tc
(Expected Benchmark Result for Page 2:) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(When asked 'How does zero-retention purge work?', the system should cite the multi-pass overwrite on Page 2.) Tj
T*
ET
