(CHAPTER 3: RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION \(RAG\) PIPELINE) Tj
T*
0 Tc
() Tj
T*
0 Tc
(3.1 RECURSIVE SEMANTIC TEXT CHUNKING) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(Documents are segmented using a recursive character splitting algorithm with a default chunk size of) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(700 characters and a 120-character sliding overlap. This ensures semantic continuity across sentence boundaries.) Tj
T*
0 Tc
() Tj
T*
0 Tc
(3.2 DUAL-MODE HYBRID VECTOR INDEX) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(The vector engine operates in two interchangeable modes:) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(- Neural Mode: Powered by Google Gemini text-embedding-004 generating 768-dimensional dense vectors.) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(- In-Memory Sparse Mode: An optimized TF-IDF and BM25 cosine similarity index that functions fully offline) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(  with zero external API dependency.) Tj
T*
0 Tc
() Tj
T*
0 Tc
(3.3 TOP-K RETRIEVAL AND RELEVANCE SCORING) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(User queries are mapped into the vector space. The retriever ranks candidates using normalized cosine) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(similarity and returns the top 4 most relevant chunks with confidence percentages.) Tj
T*
0 Tc
() Tj
T*
0 Tc
(Expected Benchmark Result for Page 3:) Tj
T*
0 Tc
(When asked 'What chunk size and overlap does the RAG pipeline use?', the system should cite 700 and 120.) Tj
T*
